<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Follow / "ambulance chase" camera toggle. Lives in the vanilla Camera category so it is
       rebindable in Options > Keyboard configuration > Camera.

       Delete, NOT Home and NOT F5. Two wrong answers before this one:
         - Home collides with TimeSpeed_Faster.
         - F5 collides with MainTab_Wildlife.
       The F5 miss is worth remembering: vanilla's function-key bindings are NOT in
       Core/Misc/KeyBindings/KeyBindings.xml. KeyBindingDefGenerator.ImpliedKeyBindingDefs() SYNTHESIZES
       a "MainTab_<defName>" KeyBindingDef for every MainButtonDef that has a <defaultHotKey>, so
       F1-F9 (Work/Schedule/Assign/Animals/Wildlife/Research/Quests/World/History) plus F10-F11 are all
       taken and only show up if you grep MainButtonDefs for defaultHotKey.

       The genuinely free space is therefore tiny: vanilla binds every letter A-Z, Alpha1-4, F1-F11,
       Home/End/Insert/PageUp/PageDown, Tab/Space/Return/Escape, the arrows, brackets, and the
       punctuation keys. Delete is unbound by vanilla, sits in the same navigation cluster as the
       camera-adjacent Home/End/Insert/PageUp/PageDown, and is not an OS/Steam default the way F12
       (Steam screenshot) is. Follow can also be toggled by right-clicking a bar cell, so this binding
       is a convenience, not the only route to the feature. -->
  <KeyBindingDef>
    <defName>RCB_FollowCam</defName>
    <!-- ⚠ The LABEL carries the mod name and the defName does NOT: renaming RCB_FollowCam would
         silently drop every player's existing binding, while the label is free to change. This one
         shipped a full release still reading "Modern Colonist Bar" - a rename leaves player-facing
         strings behind exactly where a namespace grep never reaches. -->
    <label>follow selected pawn (Radius UI)</label>
    <category>GameMapCamera</category>
    <defaultKeyCodeA>Delete</defaultKeyCodeA>
  </KeyBindingDef>

</Defs>
